\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every $1<p<infinity$, is the Fourier multiplier $(1-|\xi |^2/R^2)_+^\delta $ uniformly bounded on $L^p(R^3)$ for all $R>0$ whenever $\delta >max(3|1/p-1/2|-1/2,0)$, with the order-zero $L^2$ case also bounded?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every $1<p<infinity$, is the Fourier multiplier $(1-|\xi |^2/R^2)_+^\delta $ uniformly bounded on $L^p(R^3)$ for all $R>0$ whenever $\delta >max(3|1/p-1/2|-1/2,0)$, with the order-zero $L^2$ case also bounded?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://londmathsoc.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1112/jlms.12401}.
